[dvystrcil/homelab] Add monthly restic restore test for claude memory backup  (model=qwen3-coder-next:latest, 41s, lane=opencode)
## Why
The claude memory is backed up via restic to TrueNAS, but there is no automated test that verifies the backup can be restored. Without periodic restore tests, a silent backup failure could go unnoticed until recovery is actually needed.

## What we know
- The claude memory is stored in `claude-personal-config` and its diary path is configured via `DIARY_PATH` ([`claude-personal-config/README.md`](claude-personal-config/README.md)).
- TrueNAS replication and restic backups are used for data protection (see [`homelab/architecture/`](homelab/architecture/) docs).
- Existing scheduled jobs like `etcd-backup`, `immich-db-backup`, `pihole-backup`, and `vaultwarden-backup` run weekly or biweekly and complete successfully ([`Live pods`](Live PODS (kubectl get pods -A, filtered))).
- There is an open issue about disaster recovery playbook including ArgoCD repos and data restore verification ([https://github.com/dvystrcil/homelab/issues/29](https://github.com/dvystrcil/homelab/issues/29)).
- A related issue notes that some scheduled checks appear green because nothing asked them to work ([https://github.com/dvystrcil/homelab/issues/1184](https://github.com/dvystrcil/homelab/issues/1184)).

## Acceptance criteria
- [ ] **AC1.** A cron job (e.g., `restic-test-restore`) runs monthly and executes `restic restore --target /tmp/restic-test-restore <snapshot-id>` against the claude memory backup location.
- [ ] **AC2.** The job fails if any file in the restored directory differs from the current live directory (via checksum comparison or diff).
- [ ] **AC3.** The job sends a Slack notification on success/failure (reuse existing alerting pattern from other backup jobs).
- [ ] **AC4.** The job cleans up `/tmp/restic-test-restore` after completion.

## Lane
opencode — reuse existing restic backup infrastructure and cron pattern from other backup jobs (e.g., etcd-backup, vaultwarden-backup), only add restore verification step.

